 "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7334, "total_tokens": 7334}}, "input": {"input": ["--- Record 951 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Authentication Method for the SAP Task Center API\nDescription: You can now access the SAP Task Center API by utilizing direct authentication via SAP Cloud Identity Services - Identity Authentication.  For more information, see Access the SAP Task Center API Using Identity Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-07\nValid as Of: 2025-05-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 952 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Commercial Plan build-default Available for SAP Task Center\nDescription: A new service plan build-default is available for SAP Task Center. For more information, see Service Plans and Metering.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-07\nValid as Of: 2025-05-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 953 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Configurations API – Return Context and Source\nDescription: When creating a new configuration, the context for the reference characteristics and the source of the configuration can be specified. Both, context and source, can also be overwritten using the corresponding endpoint.   Context and source used to be missing in the configuration results. Both can now be requested as part of the configuration results by listing them in the $select query parameter like this: $select=context,source.  See  API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Pre-Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 954 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Configurations API – Return Dependencies That Caused the Conflict\nDescription: Conflicts returned by GET /configurations/{configurationId} will include the new response structure dependencyId with a list of dependencies, such as constraints, that caused the conflict.  See  API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Pre-Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 955 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Extensions Concept – WHERE LIKE Database Access\nDescription: There is a new API called sap.db() to read table content from local extensions, it will support wildcards with LIKE operator in WHERE clauses of SELECT statements.   See Extension Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Pre-Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 956 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production – Knowledge Bases API – Search By BOM Application\nDescription: There is a new filter value called bomApplication for endpoint GET /kbdetermination, which enables the search for knowledge bases by the BOM application, for example SD01 or PP01.   See  API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Pre-Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 957 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Pre-Production- Configurations API – Lock Configurations Against Changes\nDescription: There is a new endpoint called PATCH /configurations/{configurationId}/lock to flag a configuration as locked or not locked. The default setting is not locked. If a configuration is locked, it cannot be deleted, nor changed. For example, adding or removing a characteristic value or resetting the configuration is not possible.  Existing endpoints such as GET /configurations/{configurationId} will be enhanced to return the locked flag for a configuration.   The existing endpoint GET /externalConfigurations will be enhanced to allow searching for locked configurations.  See  API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing - Pre-Production.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-15\nValid as Of: 2025-05-07\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 958 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Istio module: Update to version 1.17.0\nDescription: We've updated the Istio version to 1.25.1 (#1365). Read the Istio 1.25.1 release announcement and Istio 1.25 Upgrade Notes.  This version of Istio includes changes to compatibility version parameters. See the parameters of the previous compatibility version switched from false to true:  ENABLE_INBOUND_RETRY_POLICY: If true, enables retry policy for inbound routes, which automatically retries any requests that were reset before reaching the intended service.  EXCLUDE_UNSAFE_503_FROM_DEFAULT_RETRY: If true, excludes unsafe retry on 503 from the default retry policy.  PREFER_DESTINATIONRULE_TLS_FOR_EXTERNAL_SERVICES: If true, external services prefer the TLS settings from DestinationRules over the metadata TLS settings.  ENABLE_ENHANCED", " compatibility version switched from false to true:  ENABLE_INBOUND_RETRY_POLICY: If true, enables retry policy for inbound routes, which automatically retries any requests that were reset before reaching the intended service.  EXCLUDE_UNSAFE_503_FROM_DEFAULT_RETRY: If true, excludes unsafe retry on 503 from the default retry policy.  PREFER_DESTINATIONRULE_TLS_FOR_EXTERNAL_SERVICES: If true, external services prefer the TLS settings from DestinationRules over the metadata TLS settings.  ENABLE_ENHANCED_DESTINATIONRULE_MERGE: If enabled, Istio merges DestinationRules based on their exportTo fields. The DestinationRules are then kept as independent rules if the exportTo fields are not equal.  PILOT_UNIFIED_SIDECAR_SCOPE: If true, unified SidecarScope creation is used. This is only intended as a temporary feature flag for backward compatibility.  ENABLE_DEFERRED_STATS_CREATION: If enabled, Istio lazily initializes a subset of the stats.  BYPASS_OVERLOAD_MANAGER_FOR_STATIC_LISTENERS: If enabled, the overload manager is not applied to static listeners.    This compatibility version applies the following new parameter set to false:   PILOT_ENABLE_IP_AUTOALLOCATE: If enabled, the pilot starts a controller that assigns IP addresses to ServiceEntry that do not have a user-supplied IP. When combined with DNS capture, this allows TCP routing of traffic sent to the ServiceEntry.    Note the significant changes announce with release 1.25.1 of Istio:   ISTIO_META_DNS_AUTO_ALLOCATE in proxyMetadata has been deprecated in favor of a newer version of DNS auto-allocation.  traffic.sidecar.istio.io/kubevirtInterfaces has been deprecated in favor of istio.io/reroute-virtual-interfaces.  \nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-04-18\nValid as Of: 2025-05-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 959 ---\nComponent: SAP Omnichannel Promotion Pricing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Root Certificate Replacement in the SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Environment\nDescription: Update: After an internal validation, the timelines have been shifted to Q1/2026. SAP will provide detailed dates in October 2025.  SAP is switching to the \"DigiCert TLS RSA4096 Root G5\" and “DigiCert Global Root G3” PKI.  If you have systems in which you manage the trusted certificates yourself, check if the \"DigiCert Global Root G2\" certificate exists in them. If it exists and the usage is related to SAP BTP products, please add the new G5 and G3 certificates. Do not remove the G2 certificate yet, as it is needed during the transition period.  For more information, see 3566727  and SAP BTP Cloud Foundry: switching to higher security level Root Certificate Authority.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-26\nValid as Of: 2025-05-06\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 960 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: IBM MQ Adapter Supports New Version\nDescription: A new version 1.1.0 (JMS Variant) of the IBM MQ adapter is available now.  See: IBM MQ Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-06\nValid as Of: 2025-05-06\nVersion: 2503\n\n", "--- Record 1481 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Support X.509 Certificates\nDescription: For getting an oauth token to call an endpoint of the Pricing service it used to be required to specify the client id and the client secret. Instead of the client secret, an X.509 certificate can now be used.  Action: Using X.509 certificates is considered more secure than using client id and client secret. Therefore, it is recommended to use the new approach.   See: Security Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing and Administration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1482 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production -Support X.509 Certificates\nDescription: For getting an oauth token to call an endpoint of the Variant Configuration service it used to be required to specify the client id and the client secret. Now, instead of the client secret, an X.509 certificate can be used.  Action: Using X.509 certificates is considered more secure than using the client id and client secret. Therefore, it is recommended to use the new approach.   See: Security Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing and Administration Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1483 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Configurations API – Read Single Characteristics\nDescription: There is a new endpoint called GET /api/v2/configurations/{configurationId}/items/{itemId}/characteristics used to read the details of one or more characteristics of an item.   Action: If the UI of the consuming application allows it, it is recommended to always read the configuration results during interactive configuration without the possible values of characteristics. This can be achieved by using the parameter $select omitting the parameter value possibleValue when creating or reading a configuration. Only when the user clicks on a UI element, like a dropdown list box, that requires to render the possible values on the UI, the possible values should be read for that characteristic using the new endpoint. This will improve performance especially when AVC Forwarding is enabled.   See: API Definition and Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Recommended\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1484 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 2.10.3\nDescription: The API Gateway module in version 2.10.3 includes the following changes:  We’ve changed the hardcoded algorithm from RSA256 to RS256. This change ensures that JWT tokens are processed correctly by the Ory Oathkeeper, resolving the error message signing key 'XXX' declares unsupported algorithm \"RSA256\".  If you expose a path using a wildcard pattern, now you can also expose the same path without including the trailing slash. For example, if you have a rule that exposes example.com/path/*, you can also expose example.com/path without the slash at the end.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-04\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1485 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: Telemetry module: Update to version 1.32.0\nDescription: The new version brings the following improvements:      Metrics: A more sophisticated CRD defaulting mechanism improves the sync behaviour for CI/CD tooling (#1737).      Traces and Metrics: Fixed false positive pipeline health indications (#1410).    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-22\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1486 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Correct Reporting of Service Usage\nDescription: The service usage used to be reported incorrectly if a PATCH request was sent via a POST request using the X-HTTP-Method-Override header. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-31\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1487 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Base Calculations Include Current Percentage Step\nDescription: In scenarios where a percentage condition spans multiple counters within the same step range in the pricing procedure, the condition base used not to be dynamically adjusted to account for the cumulative effect of prior conditions. Instead, all counters for the condition type used to use the original base amount. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1488 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Standard Requirement Formula 58\nDescription: Support standard", " Instead, all counters for the condition type used to use the original base amount. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1488 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Standard Requirement Formula 58\nDescription: Support standard requirement formula 58 that returns true if the accounting indicator (KOMP-BEMOT) is not initial.  See: Supported Standard Pricing Exits. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1489 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Standard Requirement Formula 67\nDescription: Support standard requirement formula 67 that always returns true in the context of the Pricing service.  See: Supported Standard Pricing Exits.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1490 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Access Sales Records in Purchasing Tables\nDescription: Only condition tables and condition records with application ‘V’ (Sales) are considered by the Pricing service. For cases where condition records with application ‘V’ were stored in condition tables with application ‘M’ (Purchasing), those tables can now be added to the replication and will also be considered.  See: Development Guide for SAP Variant Configuration and Pricing.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-12-17\nValid as Of: 2025-02-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1391 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: User Email Addresses in Tasks of Type Workflow\nDescription: Email addresses of users involved or interested in a task can now also be mapped in SAP Advanced Financial Closing for tasks of the type Workflow. As with the other parameter mappings, you need to consider the mapping requirements.  More information:  Integration of Tasks of Type Workflow  How to Create Workflows in SAP Build Process Automation and Integrate Them into the Financial Close    Area affected: Integration with SAP Build Process Automation\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-03\nValid as Of: 2025-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1392 ---\nComponent: SAP Health Data Services for FHIR\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: mTLS compliance for EMS Service Instance\nDescription: User-defined EMS instances must support mTLS. Refer to Enabling mTLS for EMS Service Instance for guidance on updating the instance to enable mTLS compliance and the additional steps needed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1393 ---\nComponent: SAP Health Data Services for FHIR\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support for certificate authentication\nDescription: SAP Health Data Services for FHIR now supports X.509 certificate-based authentication via the Cloud Identity service.   Refer to Certificate Authentication for more information. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1394 ---\nComponent: SAP Health Data Services for FHIR\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Update service instances\nDescription: You can now update a service instance of SAP Health Data Services for FHIR with an event mesh instance.  Refer to Updating Service Instances for more information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-02-16\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1395 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Process Automation\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Guided Process\nDescription: You can now delete one or more guided process instances using a simple API call. See Deletion of Personal Data-Guided Process.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-15\nValid as Of: 2025-02-15\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1396 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ABAP Cross Trace: Exporting and Importing a Trace Result\nDescription: You can now export/import a trace result of the ABAP Cross Trace to/from a JSON file. This enables you to store important trace results on a file system and to collaborate with other colleagues on error analysis.  See      Exporting an ABAP Cross Trace Result and      Importing an ABAP Cross Trace Result.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1397 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: ABAP Memory Snapshot\nDescription: You can now use the ABAP Memory Snapshot view that lists all memory snapshots. From here, you can open an ABAP memory snapshot in the editor. In the editor, the Memory Objects tab displays a list with the memory objects ranked by their size.  See  ABAP Memory Snapshots.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1398 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: AMDP Test Double Framework\nDescription: You can now write automated tests for your ABAP Managed Database Procedure (AMDP) using the new AMDP test double framework. AMDP test double framework helps in testing the logic written in an AMDP while writing the ABAP Unit tests. This API-based framework can be used to isolate and test the logic encapsulated within an AMDP method by isolating the AMDP from all the actual dependencies associated with the code being tested and replacing these dependencies with test doubles created for them.  See  AMDP Test Double Framework.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1399 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: CDS External Entity in Data Preview\nDescription: The CDS external entity is now supported in Data Preview.  See  Configuring Select Options for Data Preview Result.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP", ": ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: CDS External Entity in Data Preview\nDescription: The CDS external entity is now supported in Data Preview.  See  Configuring Select Options for Data Preview Result.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n--- Record 1400 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse: CDS Test Double Framework: Supported Test Scenario\nDescription: CDS test double frameworks now supports testing of CDS Hierarchy view.  See  ABAP CDS Test Double Framework.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-14\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2502\n\n", "--- Record 1241 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: SAML 2.0 Configuration\nDescription: The SAML 2.0 configuration page on application level has been refactored. Now you can separately configure the metadata and certificates setting. See Configure SAML 2.0 Service Provider.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: 27566\n\n--- Record 1242 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Support for externalId in UUID format\nDescription: When provisioning users to SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition, the externalId must be in UUID format.  See SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: 27566\n\n--- Record 1243 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: User Attributes\nDescription: Cloud Identity Services now supports a new local user attribute - Application Groups to list the application-specific groups to which the user is assigned to. See Configuring User Attributes from the Identity Directory.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: 27566\n\n--- Record 1244 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: User Attributes\nDescription: The name of the Groups user attribute is renamed to All Groups. See Configuring User Attributes from the Identity Directory.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: 27566\n\n--- Record 1245 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Warning of unsupported entity\nDescription: A warning message alerts you when adding an unsupported entity - such as a user, group, or role - in the transformations. While the entity will be accepted, it will not be applied.  See Manage Transformations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: 27566\n\n--- Record 1246 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New LeanIX Adapter Available\nDescription: LeanIX Receiver adapter is available now.  See: LeanIX Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: 2501\n\n--- Record 1247 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: No restart for failed job\nDescription: If a provisioning job from a source system to multiple target systems stops due to an error in one of the targets, it will not resume for that specific target upon restart. Previously, the job would continue after a restart.  For more information, see: Monitor Provisioning Job Logs\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1248 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Support for externalId in UUID format\nDescription: When provisioning users to SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition, the externalId must be in UUID format.  For more information, see: SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1249 ---\nComponent: Identity Provisioning\nEnvironment: Neo\nTitle: Warning of unsupported entity\nDescription: A warning message alerts you when adding an unsupported entity - such as a user, group, or role - in the transformations. While the entity will be accepted, it will not be applied.  For more information, see: Manage Transformations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1250 ---\nComponent: Integration Advisor\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Neo\nTitle: Overlay Mapping Guidelines\nDescription: You can now create overlay Mapping Guidelines allowing you to customize and extend base Mapping Guidelines. See Creating an Overlay Mapping Guideline.  As Cloud Integration (standalone) customer, see Creating an Overlay Mapping Guideline\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-03-11\nValid as Of: 2025-03-11\nVersion: 2501\n\n", "--- Record 611 ---\nComponent: SAP Advanced Financial Closing\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: User Group Information\nDescription: On several screens where you find the name of user groups (for example, a user group being assigned to a task or folder), you can now find additional information about the user group. The following information is available in a pop-over on the user group name:  User group name  User group description  Table listing the group members with the following information:  User name  User ID  Email address  Phone number (if available in the user profile)  Mobile phone number (if available in the user profile)      More information:  Legal Basis for Data Processing  Apps affected: Several apps where user group information is displayed.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Finance\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-09\nValid as Of: 2025-06-22\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 612 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: New models are supported, including Nova Premier from AWS Bedrock.For more information, see SAP Note 3437766 .\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-21\nValid as Of: 2025-06-21\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 613 ---\nComponent: SAP Translation Hub\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle:   Support for LLM-based translation in Software Translation  \nDescription:   Software translation workflow and editor: File and git projects now support LLM-based translation as additional translation provider, using Large Language Models via SAP's generative AI hub  APIs: LLM-based translation support was also added to the Translate API (synchronous) and the following project APIs: file project and git project API.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-18\nValid as Of: 2025-06-20\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 614 ---\nComponent: Application Frontend Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Availability in the SAP BTP Trial\nDescription: Application Frontend is available in the cf-us10- region of the SAP BTP trial.  Trial accounts are limited to five applications per subaccount.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-23\nValid as Of: 2025-06-19\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 615 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Shopify Receiver Adapter Available\nDescription: Shopify receiver adapter is available now. It facilitates connectivity with Shopify GrpahQL and REST Admin APIs.  See:   Shopify Receiver Adapter  Shopify GraphQL Receiver Adapter  Shopify REST Receiver Adapter.    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-19\nValid as Of: 2025-06-19\nVersion: 2504\n\n--- Record 616 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Automated Credential Request Processing\nDescription: Credential requests can now be automatically processed if the verifiable credential is already issued..\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-19\nVersion: 3.10\n\n--- Record 617 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extend DCP Presentation to Standard Changes\nDescription: The DCP presentation flow specification has changed, and we have included support for type\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-19\nVersion: 3.10\n\n--- Record 618 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Filter Credential Requests Received Based on the Status\nDescription: You can now filter the list of received credential requests by their status.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-19\nVersion: 3.10\n\n--- Record 619 ---\nComponent: Decentralized Identity Verification\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Support of the Additional Key Type Capability Invocation\nDescription: You can now use a new key type, Capability Invocation, which allows identities to generate tokens for securely sharing Verifiable Presentations.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2025-06-19\nVersion: 3.10\n\n--- Record 620 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Discontinuation of Node 18 Jobs\nDescription: Jobs that use Node 18 build tool versions no longer work.  Action: Please upgrade your jobs to newer build tool versions. See Supported Tools.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deleted\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-18\nValid as Of: 2025-06-18\nVersion: Cloud\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_785d284a555e7ec7d66bddd0103af361766a22a9731370e1e0a10a5eb6a05cd8_v2"}